  "description": "This course introduces students to the principles and practice of cryptographic techniques used in securing digital communications and data. Topics include symmetric and asymmetric encryption algorithms such as AES, RSA, and ECC; cryptographic hash functions like SHA-256 and SHA-3; key exchange protocols such as Diffie-Hellman; digital signatures using DSA and ECDSA; secure communication protocols such as TLS/SSL; and cryptographic standards such as PKCS #1 and RFC 5246. Students will also explore cryptographic attacks including brute-force, side-channel, and man-in-the-middle attacks, and the role of cryptographic libraries such as OpenSSL and Bouncy Castle in implementing secure systems.",
